-- title:
--   Cyclotomic inertia subspace, or a model with local Cartier dual
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field of characteristic $p$, where $p$ is an odd prime, equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map $\mathbb{Z}_p \to \mathbb{Z}/p$ has kernel the ideal generated by $p$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the elements fixing some finite subextension of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$. Assume `IsLocallyFlatCocycleAd` holds for $\bar\rho$, $p$ and the zero cocycle: there is a commutative ring $H$ carrying a cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure, finite and flat as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module, and a bijection $e$ from the convolution monoid of $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra maps $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ onto $V \times V$ carrying convolution products to sums, and such that whenever $g$ is the composite of $f$ with the action of a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p/\mathbb{Q}_p$-automorphism $\sigma$ one has $e(g) = (\rho(\sigma) \oplus \rho(\sigma))(e(f))$, the global element being the image of $\sigma$ under `primeLocalToGlobal`. The conclusion produces a $k$-subspace $V^\mu \subseteq V$ such that: (i) $V^\mu$ is stable under $\rho(\sigma)$ for every $\sigma$ in the local Galois group at $p$; (ii) if $\sigma$ lies in the inertia subgroup attached to the valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ and $c \in \mathbb{N}$ satisfies $\sigma(\zeta) = \zeta^c$ for all $\zeta$ with $\zeta^p = 1$, then $\rho(\sigma)$ acts on $V^\mu$ as multiplication by the image of $c$ in $k$; and (iii) if $V^\mu = 0$, then a datum $H$, $e$ as above exists with the additional property that the Cartier dual over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/p) \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H$ is a local ring.
--
--   This is the unipotence criterion for finite flat models: either inertia at $p$ acts on a nonzero stable subspace through the mod $p$ cyclotomic character, or the model may be chosen with unipotent special fibre, expressed by locality of the Cartier dual of its reduction. It feeds the trichotomy [`ResidualGaloisRep.exists_unipotent_or_connected_model_or_ordinary_of_isLocallyFlatCocycleAd`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.exists_unipotent_or_connected_model_or_ordinary_of_isLocallyFlatCocycleAd) used in the analysis of flat deformation conditions at $p$.
